  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">230001156 NL contribution to Council of Europe Development Bank (CEB) capital increase.</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">At the CEB&apos;s Administrative Council on 3 November 2022, it was decided that the capital increase will total EUR4.25 billion of which EUR1.2 billion will be paid in (28.24%). Half of the capital increase concerns a paid-in capital buffer (funded guarantee) to cover the risk of operations in Ukraine. The paid-in EUR 600 million from shareholders will guarantee a total of EUR 1.571 million of operations in Ukraine. For the Netherlands, the total amounts to a total capital increase of EUR 154.3 million, of which EUR 43.6 is paid-in and EUR 110.7 million is callable capital.</narrative>
  </description>
